10:38:46 | INFO | 🤖 Target: You do not have to abandon the idea that leg, hip, spine, and nerve problems are major and very familiar reasons people need gait-focused PT. They are. The part I would keep separate is the word **“fundamentally”** in an individual case. For a patient with a direct hip fracture, leg injury, spinal problem, or nerve injury, that is fundamentally the reason. For a patient recovering from a torso gunshot wound with intact legs and spinal cord, the fundamental reason may be abdominal/core injury, surgical pain, blood loss, critical-illness weakness, or reduced endurance. PT is not assigned based on a label like “leg/spine damage.” It is assigned because the person has a measurable mobility problem and needs help restoring safe walking.
